        "conclusion": "holds",
        "defect_claim": "asserted",
        "rationale": "Ten retained executions establish the account. Witness: with node 3 dropped from both halves and re-admitted, and no leader change observed, invocations on it do not return inside the observed windows (1201 ms, 800/801 ms, 900 ms, 2000 ms), release only at the caller's deadline, leave no committed payload, and are admitted unmodified once a leader change re-arms the gate (4637 ms after issue) with the payload then committed. This holds with a context that never expires, with retries, with the clock running, and under PreVote plus CheckQuorum, and the same holds for a configuration change proposed through the same member. Controls: a never-removed member returns in 0 ms and commits; a member kept as an outgoing voter of a joint configuration that is never left returns and commits; and a read-index request from the disarmed member completes with a read state while its proposal stays held, so the harm is confined to the MsgProp entry points. Source account: the run loop's gate variable is assigned only at node.go:374 (leader observed), 377 (no leader) and 426 (local member removed) and used as the receive case at node.go:386; the removal guard fires exactly when applying a conf change deletes the local Progress entry, which LeaveJoint does for outgoing voters that are in neither the incoming half nor the learner set; the snapshot's own node test scopes intended blocking to a node that does not know the current leader, which is not this case. The defect is the interval itself: a member that is a voter with a healthy, known leader cannot get proposals or configuration proposals to any decision and receives no error signal, until an unrelated leader change admits them.",
        "answers": {},
        "knowledge": [
          {
            "entry_id": "3592ccaf01864f56aaf06d54a3f97423-knowledge-0",
            "revision": 1,
            "assertion": "propc is armed only on observed leader change and is left nil after a re-admission"
          },
